  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pathways to Prosperity - Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this programme we focus on supporting the adoption of sustainable practices and ecosystem management in farming and processing for cocoa and oil palm farmers as well as gold miners as they require far and equal access to relevant technology, inputs, services as well as formalisation and certification support. Our main efforts in this programme are dedicated to developing a service delivery structure that promotes producers access to inputs, services, technology, and markets. We support (young) entrepreneurs to develop a business in service delivery and strengthen capacities of existing service providers to provide better and more inclusive services. This includes developing IT-based platforms to link smallholder farmers who demand services to providers of various services. Additionally this programme supports farmers to gain and maintain access to market information and focus on creating stronger local market opportunities by providing local processing facilities.</narrative>
  </description>
